method.description:
Shader code for erosion detail below the vertex spacing: the slope of the detail filter's next octaves (below [member detail_octaves], from [member detail_wavelength] halved per octave), differentiated analytically, with this node's seed, depth, gully weight and heights baked in. It declares [code]vec3 terrain_detail_normal(vec3 world_pos, vec3 world_normal, int octaves, float footprint)[/code], which returns the world normal with the detail added; [code]footprint[/code] is the pixel size in metres (octaves shorter than about four pixels fade out) or 0. Call it after [method generate] and paste the result into the terrain material, for example:
[codeblock lang=text]
float footprint = length(wp - CAMERA_POSITION_WORLD) * 2.0 / (PROJECTION_MATRIX[1][1] * VIEWPORT_SIZE.y);
vec3 wn = terrain_detail_normal(wp, world_normal, 4, footprint);
NORMAL = normalize((VIEW_MATRIX * vec4(wn, 0.0)).xyz);
[/codeblock]
